{
  "id": "ch-diffeq",
  "chapterNumber": "8",
  "title": {
    "en": "Differential Equations",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A differential equation relates a function to its own rate of change. Solving one means finding every function whose derivative behaves as prescribed — the language in which growth, cooling, and motion are written.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 8.1 — Differential equation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "An equation involving an unknown function and its derivatives, such as \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=f(x,y) \\). A <strong>solution</strong> is a function \\( y(x) \\) that satisfies it; an initial condition picks out one particular solution.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Separable equations.</strong> If \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=g(x)\\,h(y) \\), gather each variable on its own side and integrate:</p>\\[ \\int \\frac{dy}{h(y)}=\\int g(x)\\,dx. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Theorem 8.2 — Exponential model",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "The equation \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dt}=ky \\) has solution \\( y=y_0\\,e^{kt} \\): exponential growth when \\( k&gt;0 \\) and decay when \\( k&lt;0 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A <strong>slope field</strong> draws the prescribed slope at a grid of points; solution curves simply flow along it. Pick an equation and slide the initial value — the amber curve threads through the field from \\( (0,\\,y_0) \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Slope field &amp; solution curve",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "slopeCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A slope field with a solution curve",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "slopeDataBtn",
          "panelId": "slopeDataPanel",
          "descId": "slopeDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "slopeDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on the solution curve through (0, y₀)",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "slopeFn",
            "label": {
