              },
              {
                "value": "xmy",
                "label": "dy/dx = x − y"
              }
            ],
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Equation",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "slopeY0",
            "label": {
              "en": "Initial value &nbsp; <b>y(0) =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -3,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 0.5,
            "valueDisplayId": "slopeY0v",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Initial value y(0)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "slopeEq",
            "label": {
              "en": "equation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "dy/dx = y"
          },
          {
            "id": "slopeNote",
            "label": {
              "en": "solution through (0, y₀)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A — Separable",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=2xy \\).</p><p>Separate and integrate: \\( \\displaystyle\\int\\frac{dy}{y}=\\int 2x\\,dx \\), so \\( \\ln|y|=x^2+C \\). Exponentiating,</p>\\[ y=C e^{\\,x^2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.B — Initial value problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=3y \\) with \\( y(0)=4 \\).</p><p>By the exponential model \\( y=y_0 e^{kt} \\) with \\( k=3 \\), and \\( y(0)=4 \\):</p>\\[ y=4e^{3x}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Ordinary differential equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A differential equation relates a function to its derivatives. Separable ODEs are solved by separating variables and integrating both sides.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Separable ODE",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=g(x)h(y) \\Rightarrow \\int\\dfrac{dy}{h(y)}=\\int g(x)\\,dx \\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "wide": true
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponential growth",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y'=ky \\Rightarrow y=y_0 e^{kt} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Integrating factor",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( y'+P(x)y=Q(x) \\), \\( \\mu=e^{\\int P\\,dx} \\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "wide": true
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Logistic model",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{dP}{dt}=kP\\!\\left(1-\\dfrac{P}{M}\\right) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=2xy \\), \\( y(0)=3 \\).</p>\\[ \\int\\frac{dy}{y}=\\int 2x\\,dx \\implies \\ln|y|=x^2+C \\implies y=3e^{x^2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
